 "note": "Cases built from entities/entity_mutation.rs validate_all_merged_field_usage (ORB_E_MERGED_FIELD_UNREFERENCED). The programs are resolved .orb fixtures and the expected findings are the ones the core checks report (`program/validate`). The first step of each case is the pattern registry the rule hears (the pattern props that require entity fields: calendar-grid `events`, counter-template `entity`). The first case merges fields onto MfE that are used by a trait read or set, a tick guard, a config default, a render-ui node of a pattern requiring them, an entity contract, a persist create and a persist batch create and a fetch include from a trait linked to another entity; it leaves b, j (a persist update names its row id, not its data, in the data position), k (read as @entity.k by a trait of another entity) and deleted (a batch delete names no data) unreferenced. The second case is the control: a bare fetch or a delete-only batch names the entity with no data, so every field survives.",
